# Copy to .env and fill in. .env is gitignored.
#
# ⚑ YOU PROBABLY DO NOT NEED THIS FILE AT ALL. Configure the provider ONCE at the repo root
# (<repo>/.env) and every kit inherits it, including the ones that do not exist yet. A kit-local
# .env is an OVERRIDE, and it is merged key by key -- so a file holding only MODEL points this one
# kit at a different model and keeps the shared provider, base URL and key.
#
# THEIR PROVIDER, NOT OURS. Use whichever provider you already hold a key for -- a kit that
# hardcodes one vendor is broken for most of the people who fork it. PROVIDER picks the adapter,
# MODEL picks the model behind it, and swapping either is this file plus one more run.
#
# You do NOT need a key to see the kit work. The corpus and the recorded results ship in the repo,
# so `python -m src.app` renders and stays browsable offline -- with no key it returns a plain
# sentence saying nothing was called, rather than an error. A key is needed only to adjudicate a
# NEW claim or to re-run the eval against your own numbers.
#
# The free floor needs nothing either: `python -m evals.run --run-id b000-rules --baseline` scores
# the whole corpus with no key, no model and no spend.

PROVIDER=openai-compatible
BASE_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1
API_KEY=
MODEL=

# There is no index and no retrieval step in this kit, so no embedding model is used. Left here
# because src/config.py reads the same five variables for every kit in this repo; leave it blank.
EMBED_MODEL=
